# Claude Code configuration
CLAUDE.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials. This repository is public, so anything matching these patterns
# would be published the moment it was staged.
#
# Nothing here has ever been committed — verified with `git ls-files` — but until
# now the only safeguard was remembering to stage explicit paths, across a working
# tree with roughly 1,700 untracked files. A single `git add -A` would have
# published live Firebase credentials for four separate apps. That is a habit
# standing in for a rule; this is the rule.
#
# If one of these ever does get committed, adding it here afterwards does NOT
# help — git keeps the blob forever. Rotate the credential instead, as was
# necessary for SECRET_KEY.
*service_account_key.json
*serviceAccountKey.json
service-account*.json
*.pem
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
!staticfiles/**/*.key

# The development database. Contains real user rows, and is regenerated locally
# from migrations anyway.
db.sqlite3
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite

# Secrets loaded by load_dotenv(). .env is already ignored above; these catch the
# variants people reach for when juggling environments.
.env.*
!.env.example
